## How to Choose a Marquise Diamond Wedding Band

[![Alternating marquise diamond wedding band in 14k rose gold](/images/marquise-wedding-band-alternating-rose-gold.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings?stoneShape=marquise&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

The right band for a marquise engagement ring has three qualities. It contours to the marquise shape. It matches the ring in metal and width. And it gives clearance to the V-prong tips.

Beyond those requirements, the decision comes down to accent style. Do you want diamonds in your wedding band? Do you want a plain polished band? Do you want milgrain edge detail?

These choices do not affect fit. They affect look and price. A plain curved band starts around $539. A curved band with diamond accents starts around $790.

### Contour Bands vs. Shadow Bands

A **contour band** follows the curve of your engagement ring's shank. It is purpose-built to sit against a specific ring profile. The inner edge mirrors the outer curve of your engagement ring.

A **shadow band** — sometimes called a fitted band — follows your specific center stone setting's shape. For a marquise, it has a notch at the top that mirrors the ring's profile.

A contour band is the safer choice. It fits any marquise ring from the same metal and width family. A shadow band is ring-specific. If you resize your engagement ring, the shadow band may not fit anymore.

For most shoppers, a contour band is the right answer.

### Plain vs. Diamond-Accented Bands

A plain contour band in 14k gold starts around $539. It is elegant, durable, and matches any marquise ring style.

A diamond-accented contour band adds stones along the top face of the band. The accents continue the sparkle of your center stone visually. Prices start around $690 and rise to $1,200+ depending on total carat weight.

If your marquise engagement ring has a pavé shank, a diamond-accented band creates a seamless look. If your ring has a plain shank, either option works.

