## Metal Matching for Marquise Wedding Bands

Metal matching is not optional for marquise pairs. The center stone's visual impact depends on the entire look reading as one unified piece.

### White Gold vs. Platinum

Both look similar in the showroom. White gold requires rhodium plating every 12–18 months to maintain its bright white appearance. Platinum is naturally white and does not require plating.

Platinum costs 15–25% more for a wedding band. If you have a platinum engagement ring, match it with platinum. If your ring is white gold, white gold is fine — just budget for annual polishing.

### Rose Gold Pairing Rules

Rose gold is the most popular choice for marquise wedding bands in {{year}}. The warm pink tone complements the marquise shape's length beautifully.

One rule: do not mix 14k rose gold with 18k rose gold. The copper content difference means the pink hue is slightly different. At 14k, rose gold has a brighter pink. At 18k, it has a deeper, more muted rose. Side by side on the same finger, the difference is visible.

If your engagement ring is 18k rose gold, buy an 18k rose gold band. Period.

### Yellow Gold Pairing Rules

Yellow gold marquise bands are experiencing strong growth in {{year}}. The warm tone makes G-H color marquise diamonds appear more white. Yellow gold acts as a reference point — everything next to it looks whiter by comparison.

If your marquise is H or I color, a yellow gold band improves how the stone looks. It is one of the most underused pairing techniques out there.

