## Sizing a Marquise Diamond Wedding Band

Sizing a marquise wedding band follows the same rules as any band. There is one extra consideration.

Contour bands have a curved profile on the inner upper edge. When you resize them (up or down), the jeweler must maintain that curve's geometry. A careless resize can flatten the contour, creating a gap at the wing tip area.

Always take your wedding band to a jeweler who has seen contour bands before. Ask them specifically: "Can you maintain the contour profile during the resize?" If they pause, find another jeweler.

The other sizing note: rings stack. Your engagement ring and wedding band together add approximately 1.5–2mm of combined width. That pushes both rings slightly tighter. When wearing both rings, many people need their band sized 0.25 above their measured ring size.

Buy the wedding band slightly large if you are unsure. You can always size down. Sizing a contour band down is simpler than sizing it up.

### The Band-to-Stone Size Relationship

The marquise center stone's length determines which band width looks best. This table shows the right band width range for common marquise stone sizes.

| Marquise Stone Length | Recommended Band Width | Why This Works | What this means |
|----------------------|----------------------|----------------|-----------------|
| 8mm (0.50 ct) | 1.5mm–1.8mm | Thin band keeps the small stone as the focus | Wider band at this size swamps the center visually |
| 10mm (1.00 ct) | 1.8mm–2.2mm | Standard width matches standard solitaire shank | Ideal range for most engagement ring shanks at this size |
| 12mm (1.50 ct) | 2.0mm–2.5mm | Slightly wider band balances the longer stone | Under 2.0mm looks too delicate against a 1.5ct stone |
| 14mm (2.00 ct) | 2.2mm–2.8mm | The 2ct+ stone benefits from a more substantial band | Do not go narrower than 2.0mm at this size |

**Verdict:** The 1.0ct marquise with a 2.0mm band is the most common and most balanced pairing. If your stone is significantly larger, scale the band up proportionally. A 2.0ct marquise with a 1.6mm band looks like the tail wagging the dog.

