## Frequently Asked Questions

### Does a marquise diamond need a special wedding band?

Yes. A marquise diamond's pointed tips mean a standard straight band will leave a gap at each tip. You need a contour or curved band that mirrors the shape of your engagement ring's profile. Standard straight bands work for round, cushion, and princess center stones. They do not work for marquise.

### What width wedding band looks best with a marquise engagement ring?

Match the band width to your engagement ring's shank width within ±0.3mm. Most marquise engagement rings have shanks between 1.8mm and 2.2mm wide. A 2.0mm band is the most versatile choice. Do not go more than 0.5mm wider than your shank. That shifts focus from the center stone.

### Can I wear a straight wedding band with a marquise engagement ring?

Technically yes, but it creates two problems. First, a visible gap forms at both wing tips — wide enough to trap debris. Second, the engagement ring is not cradled, so the center stone is more prone to rotation. A contour band solves both problems for around $30–$100 more than a comparable straight band.

### How do I know if a wedding band will damage my marquise ring's prongs?

Check the Prong Clearance Zone. The inner upper edge of the band must clear your V-prong bases by 0.5mm to 1.0mm. Ask the retailer for the inner shank profile measurement at the V-prong area. Or request a side-profile image of the ring to estimate clearance yourself. A contour band for marquise rings meets this standard by default.

### What metal should I choose for a marquise wedding band?

Match your engagement ring exactly — same metal type, same color, same karatage. Pairing 14k with 18k causes karatage drift. The 14k metal dulls faster. Within 6 months the color difference is visible.

### How much should I spend on a marquise diamond wedding band?

A quality contour band with diamond accents starts at $539. The range runs to $1,200+ depending on carat total weight and metal type. For most marquise engagement rings in the $2,500–$6,000 range, a $539–$990 wedding band is proportionally appropriate. Do not underspend on the band — it lives next to your most-worn ring every day.

### Are lab diamond wedding bands a good choice for a marquise ring?

Yes. Lab diamond bands cost 30–40% less than natural bands with identical visual results. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) grades lab diamonds the same way as natural diamonds. If your center stone is natural, the origin of accent stones is invisible. Lab bands make strong financial sense here.

### Can a marquise wedding band be resized?

Yes, with one caution. Contour bands have a curved inner profile that must be maintained during a resize. A standard resize that flattens the contour recreates the gap you bought the band to prevent. Always confirm the jeweler can maintain contour geometry before authorizing a resize.

### How many diamonds should a marquise wedding band have?

This depends on the band style. Most marquise diamond wedding bands carry between 0.20 ct. tw. and 0.50 ct. tw. of accent stones. The count depends on stone size and spacing. A 0.30 ct. tw. band typically has 15–25 stones. You want continuous sparkle from the front — not isolated diamonds with visible gaps.

### Does a marquise wedding band look good with a halo engagement ring?

Yes. A [marquise halo engagement ring](/marquise-halo-engagement-ring) already has diamonds surrounding the center stone. A contour band with accents extends that look into a full eternity-style stack. The band's outer edge should align with the halo basket's outer edge — not the inner stone diameter.

### What is the difference between a contour band and a shadow band?

A contour band follows the general curved profile of your engagement ring shank. A shadow band is custom-cut to mirror your specific setting's exact shape, including any notches for basket details. Contour bands work for most marquise rings. Shadow bands are ring-specific and more expensive. For most people, a contour band is the right choice.

### How do I clean a marquise diamond wedding band?

Warm water, a drop of dish soap, and a soft toothbrush once a week. For contour bands, clean the inner edge where the band meets the engagement ring. That is where debris accumulates. A professional ultrasonic cleaning once a year removes anything the home routine misses.

### Will my marquise wedding band match my engagement ring perfectly?

If you match metal type, metal color, and karatage exactly, the bands will read as a set. Minor variations in finish (high-polish vs. brushed) or stone size will not break the visual harmony. The metal match is the critical variable — everything else is secondary.
